---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
---

<Layout
  title="Disclaimer | ShouldISpend"
  description="Read the ShouldISpend disclaimer explaining that calculators, guides, verdicts, and pressure scores are educational estimates, not personalized professional advice."
>
  <main class="trust-page">
    <p class="eyebrow">Disclaimer</p>

    <h1>Educational Estimates Only.</h1>

    <p class="updated">Last reviewed: July 2026</p>

    <p class="intro">
      ShouldISpend provides educational calculators, spending-pressure scores,
      guides, examples, and general financial explanations. The site is designed
      to help users think through spending decisions more clearly, but it does
      not provide personalized professional advice.
    </p>

    <section>
      <h2>Not Financial, Legal, Tax, Insurance, Medical, or Investment Advice</h2>

      <p>
        The information on ShouldISpend is for general educational and
        informational purposes only. It should not be treated as financial,
        legal, tax, insurance, medical, investment, lending, credit, or debt
        settlement advice.
      </p>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend is not a financial planning firm, lender, credit counselor,
        insurance agency, investment adviser, law firm, tax preparer, medical
        provider, or debt-relief company. No page on this site creates a
        professional-client relationship.
      </p>

      <p>
        Users should consult qualified professionals when a decision involves
        large debts, legal obligations, taxes, insurance claims, medical bills,
        bankruptcy risk, long-term contracts, or other complex personal
        circumstances.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>How to Use Calculator Results</h2>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend calculators use simplified assumptions and the information
        entered by the user. A result may describe a decision as comfortable,
        manageable, aggressive, or risky, but that verdict is only a general
        estimate based on the inputs provided.
      </p>

      <p>
        A low-pressure result does not mean a purchase is automatically wise.
        A high-pressure result does not mean a purchase is impossible or never
        necessary. The calculators are intended to highlight tradeoffs, not make
        final decisions for users.
      </p>

      <p>
        Users are responsible for checking the numbers they enter and deciding
        whether the result fits their full situation. Local costs, taxes,
        family obligations, job stability, credit terms, insurance coverage,
        health needs, and emergency risks may all affect the real-world outcome.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Accuracy and Updates</h2>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend aims to provide useful, practical, and clear information.
        However, calculator formulas, examples, assumptions, and explanations
        may be incomplete, outdated, simplified, or different from a user's
        exact circumstances.
      </p>

      <p>
        The site may update pages, calculators, links, examples, or assumptions
        over time. ShouldISpend does not guarantee that every calculator result,
        guide, estimate, or recommendation-style explanation will apply to every
        person or remain current forever.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>No Guarantees</h2>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend does not guarantee financial outcomes. Using a calculator
        or reading a guide cannot guarantee that a user will avoid debt, qualify
        for financing, receive assistance, save money, reduce expenses, or make
        the best possible decision.
      </p>

      <p>
        Financial decisions involve risk. Users should consider their full
        financial picture and use ShouldISpend as one educational input among
        other sources of information and judgment.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Third-Party Links and Services</h2>

      <p>
        ShouldISpend may link to third-party websites, tools, services, data
        sources, or resources. Those links are provided for convenience and
        context. ShouldISpend does not control third-party sites and is not
        responsible for their content, policies, accuracy, pricing, or actions.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section>
      <h2>Related Trust Pages</h2>

      <p>
        For more context, read the <a href="/about/">About</a> page,
        <a href="/methodology/">Methodology</a>, and
        <a href="/privacy-policy/">Privacy Policy</a>. Questions or corrections
        can be sent through the <a href="/contact/">Contact</a> page.
      </p>
    </section>
  </main>

  <style>
    .trust-page {
      max-width: 880px;
      margin: 0 auto;
      padding: 72px 24px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      color: #0f766e;
      font-weight: 800;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
      font-size: 0.8rem;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    h1 {
      font-size: clamp(2.4rem, 6vw, 4.4rem);
      line-height: 1;
      margin: 0 0 24px;
      color: #061126;
    }

    h2 {
      margin-top: 44px;
      margin-bottom: 14px;
      color: #061126;
      font-size: 1.75rem;
      line-height: 1.2;
    }

    p {
      color: #475569;
      line-height: 1.8;
      font-size: 1.05rem;
      margin-bottom: 18px;
    }

    .intro {
      font-size: 1.16rem;
      color: #334155;
    }

    a {
      color: #0f766e;
      font-weight: 700;
    }
  </style>
</Layout>
